diff --git a/docs/drivers/ath12k-wifi.md b/docs/drivers/ath12k-wifi.md
index c6bc39d..63de5d9 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/ath12k-wifi.md
+++ b/docs/drivers/ath12k-wifi.md
@@ -89,3 +89,23 @@ Device verification covers Wi-Fi toggling, SSID scanning, WPA2 association,
 DHCP, traffic and join-result delivery. Current device checks pending:
 cancellation/timeout completion, signal display, Data firmware startup,
 throughput, jitter and heat. See the [sheng network record](/devices/sheng#network).
+
+For a clean sheng build, `python3 scripts/fetch-wifi-firmware.py` fetches missing
+WCN7850 inputs from the immutable source recorded in the board manifest. The
+userspace builder invokes it before staging. Length and SHA-256 must match the
+existing pins; a different local file is rejected. `--check` verifies local
+inputs without a download. Firmware binaries remain outside Git.
+
+The sheng firmware-reader host fixture covers all existing allowed names,
+including `amss2.bin` and the optional unattended-test `join.txt`, and rejects
+unknown names and path traversal. It prints sanitizer and assertion diagnostics
+on failure. This fixture does not perform radio or network operations.
+
+The sheng userspace builder resolves the component's locked sources with
+`tools/fetch-sources.py` before building the supplicant. A clean checkout has
+no `deps/` tree; `--check` alone cannot prepare it. The package workflow builds
+and signs the iOS Wi-Fi layer before the long runtime preparation step.
+
+The source lock contains anchored patterns and individual files. Its fetcher
+uses `git sparse-checkout set --no-cone`; the default cone mode of a fresh
+sparse clone rejects those patterns. Dependency revisions are unchanged.
